{
  "module": "Inference: prefill, decode and the cache",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "prefill-decode",
    "title": "Prefill and decode",
    "summary": "The two phases of running a model: prefill processes the whole prompt in parallel in one pass, and decode then produces one token at a time. They are limited by different things.",
    "covers": ["prefill-vs-decode"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "generation-loop",
        "reason": "Decode is the one-token-at-a-time loop."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "stack-and-size",
        "reason": "Each phase is a whole pass through the stack of blocks."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "causal-mask",
        "reason": "The mask is why the prompt can be processed in parallel."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "two-phases",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "When you send a prompt to a model and it writes a reply, the work splits into "
            },
            {
              "text": "two phases",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": "
            },
            {
              "text": "prefill",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", then "
            },
            {
              "text": "decode",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "They are different enough that they are limited by different resources, and that is what the rest of this module is about."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 76)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "prefill",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Prefill",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " processes the "
            },
            {
              "text": "whole prompt in parallel, in one pass",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " through all the blocks. Every prompt token is already known, and the causal mask lets each position be computed without waiting for the ones after it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It also fills something called the "
            },
            {
              "text": "KV cache",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", which the next lesson explains."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 76, 20)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "decode",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Decode",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is the generation loop you already know: "
            },
            {
              "text": "one token per step, one after another",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Each new token needs its own pass, because it depends on the token chosen just before it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So the reply is built by many small passes, not by one big one."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 76, 20)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "different-limits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Prefill and decode are usually held back by different things."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Prefill",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " is typically "
              },
              {
                "text": "compute-bound",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": there is a lot of arithmetic to do, on many tokens at once, and the speed of the arithmetic is the limit."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Decode",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " is typically "
              },
              {
                "text": "memory-bandwidth-bound",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": for each single token it must read "
              },
              {
                "text": "all the model's weights",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " and the whole KV cache, so the speed of reading memory is the limit, not the arithmetic."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Both descriptions say "
            },
            {
              "text": "typically",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": the balance depends on the hardware and the sizes involved."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 76)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "counting",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A prompt of 1,000 tokens and a reply of 200 tokens:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "prefill: 1 pass over 1,000 positions"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "decode: 200 passes, each over 1 new position, so the weights are read 200 times"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The prompt is a single big step. The reply is where most of the passes are."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 76, 20)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
